{
	"format": 1,
	"_doc": "The audio seam (PLAN.md 14.1, 14.2): the ONLY place a sound ID maps to a file. Read by SoundBank, played by the Audio autoload. The files are built by tools/make_audio.py (Kenney CC0 picks and sounds synthesised there); every one is peak-normalised, so db sets how loud each plays. enemy_db: an enemy's gunfire against the player's own. Sounds in the world fade out by max_distance_u (U) from the camera along the attenuation curve. A ship big_boom_u long or more (or the player's) blows up with boom.big. Music crossfades over music_fade_s; each scene Router opens plays its music_for_scene track (default_music otherwise), and a flight plays combat.",
